<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem $480 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem $480 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Tuesday said</p>
<p>it will redeem all outstanding amounts of seven medium-term</p>
<p>note issues totalling $480 million as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip     Redemption</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number	Date</p>
<p> $150 million     7.90	07/22/04   31364A2A9   07/22/97</p>
<p> $100 million     7.11	04/16/01   31364CAZ1   06/20/97</p>
<p>  $50 million     7.13	05/21/01   31364CDA3   06/20/97</p>
<p>  $50 million     7.70	04/25/06   31364CBU1   06/20/97</p>
<p>  $50 million     7.16	04/18/01   31364CBE7   06/20/97</p>
<p>  $50 million     7.78	05/22/06   31364CDF2   06/20/97</p>
<p>  $30 million     7.75*     06/09/09   31364AU91   07/21/97</p>
<p>*Current interest rate</p>
<p>The redemption price of the notes will be 100 percent of the principal amount plus interest accrued to the redemption date, Fannie Mae said.</p>
</text>
